  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Volume contains three poems by Emily Dickinson printed in Spanish and English. Text is printed on white paper with black floral borders that have been affixed to corrugated cardboard. Boards are accordion folded revealing 6 pages within. Outside cover has been decorated with tipped in illustrations showing a red bird sitting on a branch. There is a small folded piece of brown paper with floral illustrations and the words "En voz baja / in a small voice" attached by string. Back covers decorated with flowers, butterflies, a portrait of a Emily Dickinson, and the Vigia lamp.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Part of a collection of handmade chapbooks published by Ediciones Vigía under the auspices of the Cuban Ministry of Culture.</subfield>
